## 1. Introduction
Photonics is the science of generating, controlling, and detecting light waves and photons, which plays an essential role in many fields including communication technologies, information processing, military, and biomedicine.1–3 Since photons exhibit great superiority over electrons as information carriers in terms of speed, bandwidth and capacity, photonics provides a promising solution to the current bottlenecks that limit the
